{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1486868-sin-again-daeva-bloodline-overview","id":1486868,"title":"Sin Again: Daeva Bloodline overview","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-18T05:44:33-07:00","id":1486868,"title":"Sin Again: Daeva Bloodline overview","content":"Video:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/4y84NL8Y5b4\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/4y84NL8Y5b4\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/4y84NL8Y5b4\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/4y84NL8Y5b4 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/376645/Sin-Again-Daeva?affiliate_id=3340454\" target=\"_blank\">Sin Again: Daeva PDF through Storyteller's Vault</a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\">My notes for the video:</span> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Children of Judas</span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>Flavor - These Daeva feed off of grief, remorse, or regret.</li> <li>Disciplines - Unlike normal Daevas they replace Majesty with Auspex and Nightmare as Clan Disciplines.</li> <li>Bane - Their downside is that they need to feed off of morose individuals or else gain the Deprived Condition because they haven\u2019t gotten their fix.</li> <li>Gift - Their Bloodline Gift is a Taste of Grief, which allows them to see visions of a breaking point their victim experienced.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duchagne</span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>Flavor - These Daeva need to experience strong emotion and are often called hedonists.</li> <li>Disciplines - These Daeva gain the Resilience discipline.</li> <li>Bane - But they have to have strong emotions while feeding, or else they\u2019ll experience the normal Daeva Clan bane even if they\u2019ve never fed from the prey before.</li> <li>Gift - Their Bloodline Gift is The Spice of Life which allows them to regain Willpower when feeding on someone who is experiencing extreme sensations.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Erzsebet</span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>Flavor - These Daeva appear to be alive. I asked lead developer Sam Young to help me better describe this Bloodline and he responded that they tend to be con artists who\u2019ve amassed wealth by faking it till they make it.</li> <li>Disciplines - The Daeva gain access to the Auspex Discipline.</li> <li>Bane - Unlike other vampires the Erzsebet age like mortals at slightly increased rate. When they pass the age a normal human would have died by they look the most decrepit a human could be and still be alive. They can reverse the aging process by going into torpor up to the age they were embraced.</li> <li>Gift - Their Bloodline Gift is Almost Human. They are have access to permanent blush of life and maintain most physical appearance changes through daysleep. Instead of Blush of Life, the Erzsebet can suppress their Predatory Aura, heal like a normal human, and get bonuses to interacting with humans.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gulikan</span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>Flavor - These Daevas are known as the perfumers and have an obsession for scents.</li> <li>Bane - The downside for Gilkan is that they can become obsessed with people from being around them for too long.</li> <li>Disciplines - Disciplines are unchanged, but gain access to Blood Sorcery.</li> <li>Gift - They have access to a form of Blood Sorcery known as Ortam which allows them to distill blood magic into perfumes.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Moda Mortale</span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>Flavor - Moda Mortale Devas are fashionable vampires that are actually experts in espionage.</li> <li>Disciplines - They get access to Protean and Obfuscate instead of Celerity. \\</li> <li>Bane - Their main flaw is that they can suffer emotional setbacks when they find out their plans are flawed.</li> <li>Gift - Their Bloodline gift is Finishing School. This gift gives a host of extra merits such as a Fighting Style and the Taste merit. As well as friends with kindred in other areas if they purchase the Cacophony Savvy merit.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Nelapsi</span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>Flavor - The Nelapsi Daeva are gluttonous aristocrats. <br /> <i>Sam Young, Lead Developer: W</i><i>e also sort of thought of them as &quot;medieval ghost stories&quot;, where they use spooky reputations to craft narratives in order to feed better.</i></li> <li>Disciplines - In place of Celerity they gain Nightmare and Resilience.</li> <li>Bane - Their Bloodline bane is that they have a hard time stopping when they feed to the point where they will vomit up the excess that they cannot store.</li> <li>Gift - Their Bloodline Gift are the Lessons. A series of merits and devotions that they learn overtime. The Lessons make it harder to stake the Daeva, allow them to consume vitae faster, be legendarily famous, and to have a large domain where residents ignore scenes of grotesque violence.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Star-Crossed</span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>Flavor - Star-crossed are vampires with vitae that can bestow amazing gifts to those that drink of it.</li> <li>Bane - Their Bane however is that when their image is recorded or reflected it shows a monstrous image instead.</li> <li>Disciplines - In place of Vigor they gain Dominate and Resilience.</li> <li>Gift - Starcrossed have the Bloodline Gift of Purification where they can anoint a mortal with blood so that for 1 week by the end of each night the mortal returns to the state they were in the day before, even through injury and death. This turns them into an entity known as a Purity. The Purity\u2019s blood turns into a golden substance called Electrum which can be harvested and used to heal people as well as resetting a Vampire\u2019s appearance back to when they were Embraced, even if the scars are from fire and sunlight.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Xiao</span></span></b><br /><br /><ul><li>Flavor - The Xiao Daeva are a pyramid scheme.<br /> <i>Sam Young, Lead Developer: Another way of looking at them is sort of &quot;obverse&quot; Daeva. They're Serpents who spurn emotion in order to gain more control over their victims (as opposed to more typical Daeva, who revel in emotions)</i></li> <li>Bane - Their Bloodline Bane is to be unable to identify with human emotion.</li> <li>Disciplines - Along with the normal Daeva Disciplines they gain access to Nightmare.</li> <li>Gift - The Blood Gift for Xiao is the Kingjan merit. The merit allows the Daeva to suck emotions of their victims while feeding as well as negate their Bloodline Bane at the highest level for a night if they drain their victim to unconsciousness.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18