ttachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T06:06:04-07:00","id":1486991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1486868-sin-again-daeva-bloodline-overview?p=1486880#post1486880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Duchagne not illusionists anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with the 1e version. But Satchel has attached Dev notes which might be insightful.<br /> <br /> The extra Devotions the Duchagne get seem to be focused on manipulating emotion.<ul><li>Incite - Target's body response to stimuli is overloaded. Making it harder for them to use Stamina or Composure to resist effects. (GIVES THE INFLAMED CONDITION)</li> <li>Induce - Target is given a single intense emotion to distract them.</li> <li>Inure - Target is given extra dice to resistance rolls, if target has the INFLAMED condition you increase the amount of damage they need to take in order to resolve Inflamed.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member"